  <section>
    <h2>Dispensaries in Calais</h2>

    <h3>The Higher Class (Medical)</h3>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 479 Main St, Calais, ME 04619<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 952-9146<br>
    <strong>Hours:</strong> Mon 9am–7pm, Tue–Sat 10am–4pm (confirm before visiting)<br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Medical (MMMP)</p>
    <p>The Higher Class operates as a medical dispensary on Main Street in downtown Calais. It is the established medical option for Washington County's border-region patients, including those in Calais, Baileyville, Princeton, and the surrounding rural communities, and won 3rd Place for Medical Dispensary of the Year at the 2024 Maine Cannabis Expo Community Awards. <a href="https://thehigherclass420.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">thehigherclass420.com</a></p>

    <h3>Kannacopia</h3>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 38 North St, Calais, ME 04619<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> confirm via <a href="https://kannacopia.com" rel="noopener noreferrer">kannacopia.com</a><br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Medical (MMMP)</p>
    <p>Kannacopia is a medical cannabis dispensary on North Street in Calais, convenient for visitors crossing the international bridge from St. Stephen, New Brunswick. Confirm current hours and contact details on the operator's site before visiting.</p>

    <h3>Smoke On The Water / Mt. Tom Therapeutics</h3>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 376 North St, Calais, ME 04619<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 454-0444<br>
    <strong>Hours:</strong> call to confirm<br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Medical (MMMP) + smoke shop / holistic wellness</p>
    <p>Smoke On The Water operates under a dual brand with Mt. Tom Therapeutics, combining a cannabis dispensary with a smoke shop and holistic-wellness storefront on North Street. It carries flower, vapes, cartridges, and accessories, and serves medical (MMMP) customers. <a href="https://smokeonthewatertherapeutics.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">smokeonthewatertherapeutics.com</a></p>

    <h3>Pine Island Cannabis — Baring (just outside Calais)</h3>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 461 US-1 (Maine Hwy 1), Baring, ME 04694<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 454-0801<br>
    <strong>Hours:</strong> Mon–Sat ~10am–6pm, Sun ~12pm–5pm (confirm before visiting)<br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Medical (MMMP) — medical card and ID required for THC purchases</p>
    <p>Pine Island Cannabis is located in <strong>Baring</strong>, just outside Calais on US-1, not in Calais proper. It is a medical dispensary — a medical card and ID are required to purchase THC products. The store carries flower, concentrates, and edibles, with a daily happy hour. <a href="https://www.facebook.com/Pine-Island-101663588304788" rel="noopener noreferrer">Facebook</a></p>
  </section>

  <Callout title="International Border Market" type="insight">
    Calais is one of the most distinctive small-town cannabis markets in Maine: the international bridge at Calais–St. Stephen connects to New Brunswick, Canada, and Canadian border-town visitors historically account for a portion of Calais retail demand. For operators, this means the four-store market is supported not just by the local 3,000 residents but by cross-border visitors and the broader Washington County catchment. Importation of cannabis into Canada remains illegal, but adult-use tourists traveling to the U.S. side of the border routinely use Calais dispensaries.
  </Callout>

  <section>
    <h2>Calais's Market Context</h2>
    <p>Calais sits on the east bank of the St. Croix River, directly across from St. Stephen, New Brunswick — one of the easternmost U.S.-Canada land-border crossings on the East Coast. The town's downtown is built around that bridge crossing, and for over a century, the cross-border economy has been a defining feature of Calais retail. Cannabis is a natural extension of that pattern.</p>
    <p>Calais's dispensary cluster is unusually dense for a town of 3,000, and reflects three factors: (1) the cross-border visitor flow, (2) the broad rural catchment across eastern Washington County, and (3) the early opt-in by the city of Calais, which created room for the operator cluster to develop. The Higher Class anchors the medical segment, with Kannacopia and Smoke On The Water / Mt. Tom Therapeutics also serving medical patients in town, and Pine Island Cannabis just outside in Baring.</p>
    <p>Operators evaluating Washington County should treat Calais as the eastern anchor, Machias as the mid-route stop, and Ellsworth as the western gateway. All three markets are functional and distinct; the Maine NB-border region has its own cannabis geography that mirrors its 19th-century commercial geography.</p>
  </section>

